        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">an atrioventricular block AE that there is some  prolongation of AV conduction time (PR interval). The heart&apos;s electrical signals are slowed as they move from the atria to the ventricles (the heart&apos;s upper and lower chambers, respectively). This results in a longer, flatter line between the P and the R waves on the EKG (electrocardiogram). </Literal>
