        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo2:OAE_0001603</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">a second degree atrioventricular block AE that the electrical signals are delayed more and more with each heartbeat, until the heart skips a beat. On the EKG, the delay is shown as a line (called the PR interval) between the P and QRS waves. The line gets longer and longer until the QRS waves don&apos;t follow the next P wave. </Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
