        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="purl:Definition"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo2:OAE_0001892</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">Parageusia AE is a gustatory system AE which is the medical term for a bad taste in the mouth. One common form of parageusia is a metallic taste of food. This can be a side effect of several medications, such as acetazolamide, eszopiclone, zopiclone, metronidazole, or etoposide. Metallic taste is also a type of dysgeusia which is frequently associated with infections in the mouth or upper airways.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
