        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo2:OAE_0001980</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">Sinus arrest AE is an arrhythmia AE that is a medical condition wherein the sinoatrial node of the heart transiently ceases to generate the electrical impulses that normally stimulate the myocardial tissues to contract and thus the heart to beat. It is defined as lasting from 2.0 seconds to several minutes.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
