        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">T-wave inversion AE is an electrocardiogram result abnormal AE that can be a sign of coronary ischemia, Wellens&apos; syndrome, left ventricular hypertrophy, or CNS disorder. In electrocardiography, the T wave represents the repolarization (or recovery) of the ventricles.</Literal>
