        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">Fibrosing alveolitis AE is a lung  inflammation AE that is a disease of unknown cause mainly involving the gas-exchanging portions of the lungs. It may occur in isolation and be called cryptogenic or idiopathic, in which case the clinical manifestations are mainly respiratory, or it may be associated with other disorders, such as rheumatoid arthritis.</Literal>
