        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">an arrhythmia AE that is characterized by shortness of breath, heart palpitations, chest tightness, and a very fast pulse. Supraventricular arrhythmias begin in the areas above the heart’s lower chambers, such as the upper chambers (the atria) or the atrial conduction pathways.</Literal>
