        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="purl:Definition"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo2:OAE_0002501</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en" datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">An exudative retinopathy AE is an eye AE that shows an outcome of exudative retinopathy marked by masses of white or yellowish exudate in the posterior part of the fundus oculi, with deposits of cholesterol and blood debris from retinal hemorrhage, that leads to destruction of the macula and blindness.</Literal>
