        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo2:IAO_0000112"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo2:OAE_0002518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="&rdf;PlainLiteral">An infection adverse event that results in malaria, a protozoan infection caused by the genus Plasmodium. There are four species of Plasmodium that can infect humans: Plasmodium falciparum, vivax, ovale, and malariae. It is transmitted to humans by infected mosquitoes. Signs and symptoms include paroxysmal high fever, sweating, chills, and anemia.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
